{number: 112}
{title: Shall We Gather at the River}
{key: Eb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Eb] Shall we gather at the river,
Where bright angel feet have [Bb7] trod,
With its [Eb] crystal tide forever
Flowing by the [Bb7] throne of [Eb] God?
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Yes, we'll [Ab] gather at the [Eb] river,
The beautiful, the [Bb7] beautiful river;
Gather with the [Eb] saints at the [Ab] river
That [Eb] flows by the [Bb7] throne of [Eb] God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
On the [Eb] margin of the river,
Washing up its silver [Bb7] spray,
We will [Eb] walk and worship ever,
All the [Bb7] happy golden [Eb] day.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Soon we'll [Eb] reach the shining river,
Soon our pilgrimage will [Bb7] cease;
Soon our [Eb] happy hearts will quiver
With the [Bb7] melody of [Eb] peace.
{end_of_verse}
